meta {
  name: GitHub Install Callback
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/github/install-callback?state=REPLACE_WITH_SIGNED_STATE&installation_id=12345&setup_action=install
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  state: REPLACE_WITH_SIGNED_STATE
  installation_id: 12345
  setup_action: install
}

docs {
  # GitHub Install Callback (browser-driven)

  GitHub redirects the user's browser here after install/de-install. **You
  normally don't call this from Bruno** — exposed for debugging / inspecting
  the redirect target. Auth is via the signed `state` query param (no Keycloak
  token, the browser-side redirect can't carry one).

  ## Query Parameters

  - `state` (required) — HMAC-signed state from `POST /auth/github/install`
  - `installation_id` (optional integer) — the GitHub installation that was
    just created or updated. Missing when GitHub posts back without an install
    (e.g. `setup_action=request`).
  - `setup_action` (optional) — `install`, `update`, `request`, …

  ## Behavior

  - Verifies `state`. Bad/expired state → 302 to
    `{frontend_base_url}/github/connected?status=error&reason=invalid_state`.
  - `setup_action=request` → 302 with `reason=request_pending`.
  - Missing `installation_id` → 302 with `reason=missing_installation_id`.
  - Otherwise persists `users.github_installation_id` and 302s with
    `status=ok`.

  ## Returns

  Always a `302 Found` redirect to the frontend.
}
